WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.197
Use this final decision guide when you are unsure.

00:00:03.197 --> 00:00:06.857
Start from the problem, not from a favorite function.

00:00:06.857 --> 00:00:11.407
Choose the smallest operation that expresses the intended transformation.

00:00:11.407 --> 00:00:16.547
That produces SQL that is easier to read, test, and maintain.

00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:23.702
Module 9 will build on these ideas by applying broader data-cleaning strategies across complete datasets.

00:00:23.702 --> 00:00:29.122
Connect this idea to a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates.

00:00:29.122 --> 00:00:34.772
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.772 --> 00:00:42.427
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.427 --> 00:00:48.227
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:54.205
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
